WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.041
Back in town the statue was also staring at something.

2
00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:11.541
He had no choice but to stare at the town all day.

3
00:00:11.542 --> 00:00:14.796
His body was frozen in place.

4
00:00:14.797 --> 00:00:21.155
But he was alive inside his golden shell, watching people pass by.

5
00:00:21.156 --> 00:00:26.374
"Nana will pay for what's she done to me," he thought angrily.

6
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:32.988
"If I ever escape this statue, that is!"

7
00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:38.249
One morning a group of townspeople began gathering at his base.

8
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:42.785
"Here they are again!" the statue thought in frustration.

9
00:00:42.786 --> 00:00:46.541
"Every day they come and stand by me.

10
00:00:46.542 --> 00:00:50.708
And all they do is talk, talk, talk!

11
00:00:50.709 --> 00:00:56.655
Grr! I wish I had some fruit to throw at them!"

12
00:00:56.656 --> 00:01:02.082
Usually, the townspeople talked about how proud they were of the statue.

13
00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:06.582
"His gold shines!"

14
00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:11.457
"His jewels sparkle!"

15
00:01:11.458 --> 00:01:14.051
"Look at his smile.

16
00:01:14.052 --> 00:01:20.280
Seeing him makes me happy too!"

17
00:01:20.281 --> 00:01:22.750
But this day was different.

18
00:01:22.751 --> 00:01:26.319
People weren't talking about the statue's smile.

19
00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:29.801
They weren't admiring his gold or jewels.

20
00:01:29.802 --> 00:01:34.166
They were complaining—a lot!

21
00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:38.355
"I lost my farm," one man said.

22
00:01:38.356 --> 00:01:43.124
"I couldn't pay my taxes to the king."

23
00:01:43.125 --> 00:01:48.676
"I had to sell my shoes to buy food," a woman said.

24
00:01:48.677 --> 00:01:52.253
Others began calling out their problems.

25
00:01:52.254 --> 00:01:57.973
And reader, they had a lot of serious problems.

26
00:01:57.974 --> 00:02:01.082
"Grr," the statue thought.

27
00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:07.041
"If I could move my hands, I'd put them over my ears!"

28
00:02:07.042 --> 00:02:13.166
But he couldn't move. So, he had no choice but to listen.

29
00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:17.752
Soon the mayor arrived and quieted the crowd.

30
00:02:17.753 --> 00:02:21.156
"Why are you complaining?

31
00:02:21.157 --> 00:02:26.124
It was good of the king to give us this beautiful statue."

32
00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:29.981
"Exactly!" the statue thought.

33
00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:35.124
"I make this ugly town much prettier!"

34
00:02:35.125 --> 00:02:40.001
But then a girl, not much older than the prince, spoke up.

35
00:02:40.002 --> 00:02:44.864
"We like the statue. But it's not a person.

36
00:02:44.865 --> 00:02:48.916
Why does it need all that gold?"

37
00:02:48.917 --> 00:02:54.541
"Its beauty doesn't help the poor," a woman added.

38
00:02:54.542 --> 00:03:01.520
"We could buy a lot of food with those jewels!" somebody shouted.

39
00:03:01.521 --> 00:03:10.416
The girl nodded. "What good is beauty if we're poor and hungry?"

40
00:03:10.417 --> 00:03:13.624
The statue wanted to stay angry.

41
00:03:13.625 --> 00:03:17.960
But he was beginning to feel something strange and new.

42
00:03:17.961 --> 00:03:23.499
"My chest feels funny," he thought.

43
00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.087
Then he remembered something Nana had said.

44
00:03:26.088 --> 00:03:31.666
"Your heart is as cold and heavy as stone."

45
00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:36.778
"It's my heart," the statue realized.

46
00:03:36.779 --> 00:03:48.766
"Nana was right. I have a cold and heavy heart."

